From f56f6c9af418066cf6d5b17e1a5fddc8e52702ed Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 09:40:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] DiscSoftTelecineScan: Kodi closing stops the scans of a disc,
 and one left in a read touches nothing of Kodi when it comes back

The scan of the titles of a disc runs on a thread that nobody joins. Where Kodi
closed while that thread was in a read of the image that did not come back,
the thread could come back while Kodi takes down what it reads with: the
clients of the network (CApplication::Stop(): smb.Deinit(), the NFS
connection), the libraries (CSectionLoader::UnloadAll() at exit unloads
libdvdnav, which the thread is in when its read was made by libdvdread), the
log; and on its way out it would close its image (CFile) and libdvdnav
(dvdnav_close(), the DllDvdNav that it loaded): a crash at exit.

Now:
- The scans that run are counted (KODI::DISC::ScanRegistry, never freed).
  CApplication::Stop() calls CDiscSoftTelecineScan::StopAll() next to the
  other readings that it stops, before the clients of SMB and NFS go: every
  scan stops (Stopped()), none starts, the ones that run are waited for up to
  2 s, and one that is closing what it read with up to 1 s more. Where no scan
  runs, it returns at once: Kodi closes as fast as before.
- A scan still left is given up: when its read comes back (the callbacks of
  the image, the opening of it, the start of its last steps) it parks for good
  (KODI::DISC::Park()) and touches nothing of Kodi again; the process ends with
  it parked. Its log of libdvdnav says nothing once Kodi closes.
- libdvdnav stays loaded until the process ends (a reference of its own,
  never let go), for a scan of a folder whose read is made by libdvdread.
- A scan is started only for an image on this system or on a share of SMB, and
  a folder on this system. A read of SMB holds the lock of the SMB client that
  smb.Deinit() takes, so the client waits for it, as it does for a read of the
  player (at most its timeout, sambaclienttimeout). The NFS client is taken
  down under a read without waiting for it: an image on NFS is no longer read
  ahead.

t_scanexit (address and undefined behaviour sanitizers, one process a case):
with no scan the shutdown does not wait (0.1 ms); a scan in a read that comes
back after 1.5 s is left after the 300 ms of the test and touches nothing when
it comes back; a scan that reads ends within the wait and closes what it read
with first; one that closes when the wait ends is waited for (651 ms); no scan
starts once Kodi closes. Mutants: a scan that does not park touches "Kodi"
twice after the shutdown; a shutdown without a limit waits 1.4 s; one without
the moment more leaves the closing scan.
